---
source: crates/diffle/tests/cli.rs
expression: "sections.join(\"\\n\")"
---
$ diffle working --help

Same as `diffle HEAD..worktree`: uncommitted changes, staged and untracked files included.

Usage: diffle working [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -C <path>                      run as if started in <path> (any directory inside a git worktree)
  -h, --help                     display help for command
  -p, --port <port>              port to listen on (default: 4966, or the next free one; 0 = random)
  -H, --host <host>              address to bind; use 0.0.0.0 to expose on the network (default:
                                 127.0.0.1)
      --allowed-origin <origin>  trusted public HTTP(S) origin behind a reverse proxy (without a
                                 path)
      --no-open                  do not open a browser
      --keep-alive               keep the server running after all browser tabs close
      --no-watch                 do not watch for changes
      --auto-viewed <glob>       mark matching files viewed for this session (repeatable)
  -U, --context <n>              context lines around changes for this session (default: config, 5)
      --lsp <language=command>   language server command for one language, started for this run
                                 (repeatable); by default the diff's languages are served by
                                 whatever is on PATH
      --no-lsp                   do not start any language server
      --timing                   print startup phase timings to stderr

$ diffle pr --help

A GitHub pull request, as GitHub shows it: merge-base(base, head) vs head.

Usage: diffle pr [OPTIONS] [pr]

Arguments:
  [pr]  pull request number or url; default: the pull request for this branch

Options:
  -C <path>                      run as if started in <path> (any directory inside a git worktree)
  -h, --help                     display help for command
  -p, --port <port>              port to listen on (default: 4966, or the next free one; 0 = random)
  -H, --host <host>              address to bind; use 0.0.0.0 to expose on the network (default:
                                 127.0.0.1)
      --allowed-origin <origin>  trusted public HTTP(S) origin behind a reverse proxy (without a
                                 path)
      --no-open                  do not open a browser
      --keep-alive               keep the server running after all browser tabs close
      --no-watch                 do not watch for changes
      --auto-viewed <glob>       mark matching files viewed for this session (repeatable)
  -U, --context <n>              context lines around changes for this session (default: config, 5)
      --lsp <language=command>   language server command for one language, started for this run
                                 (repeatable); by default the diff's languages are served by
                                 whatever is on PATH
      --no-lsp                   do not start any language server
      --timing                   print startup phase timings to stderr

$ diffle range-diff --help

How one series of commits became another, as git range-diff shows it: the older range replayed onto
the newer one’s base against the newer range, with the commits paired.

Usage: diffle range-diff [OPTIONS] <ranges>...

Arguments:
  <ranges>...  two ranges: <a>..<b> <c>..<d>, <base> <b> <d>, or <b>...<d>

Options:
  -C <path>                      run as if started in <path> (any directory inside a git worktree)
  -h, --help                     display help for command
  -p, --port <port>              port to listen on (default: 4966, or the next free one; 0 = random)
  -H, --host <host>              address to bind; use 0.0.0.0 to expose on the network (default:
                                 127.0.0.1)
      --allowed-origin <origin>  trusted public HTTP(S) origin behind a reverse proxy (without a
                                 path)
      --no-open                  do not open a browser
      --keep-alive               keep the server running after all browser tabs close
      --no-watch                 do not watch for changes
      --auto-viewed <glob>       mark matching files viewed for this session (repeatable)
  -U, --context <n>              context lines around changes for this session (default: config, 5)
      --lsp <language=command>   language server command for one language, started for this run
                                 (repeatable); by default the diff's languages are served by
                                 whatever is on PATH
      --no-lsp                   do not start any language server
      --timing                   print startup phase timings to stderr

$ diffle config --help

print the config file path and contents

Usage: diffle config

Options:
  -h, --help  display help for command
